tags: poland_event
on-arrival: prosecution_status = "Barski remains under PiS executive backing"; prosecution_independence -= 1; news_headline = "The surviving PiS cabinet retains the inherited prosecution command"

= January 2024 — Scrutiny without command

**Dariusz Barski** remains National Prosecutor. In 2022, **Zbigniew Ziobro**,
then Justice Minister and Prosecutor General from PiS coalition partner
Solidarna Polska, restored him from retirement through a provision whose legal
use remains disputed. Because PiS
has retained the cabinet in this timeline, there is no incoming minister to
declare that restoration ineffective. Justice Minister **[+ justice_minister
+]** accepts Barski's chain of command, and Prime Minister **[+ prime_minister
+]** has no intention of opening it for the opposition.

Regional prosecutors therefore know where instructions come from. They do not
know whether a future court or government will treat those instructions as
lawful. **Jarosław Kaczyński**, PiS chair, calls continuity the end of the
matter; lawyers appearing before the prosecutors cannot afford such
confidence.

[? if left_in_government = 0: Lewica is outside the executive. It can expose
appointments, write an alternative law and organise parliamentary scrutiny,
but it cannot dismiss Barski or issue a single prosecutorial instruction. The
danger is becoming loud enough to share the blame and too weak to change the
command.?]
[? if left_in_government = 1: Lewica has entered a PiS-led cabinet, but Justice
and the prosecution remain PiS red lines. Our ministers now sit beside the
people protecting Barski without possessing the authority to replace him. The
choice is no longer whether to criticise the government from outside; it is
how much coalition peace to spend proving that participation has not become
consent.?]

- @pis_prosecution_ledger
- @pis_prosecution_statute
- @pis_prosecution_committee

@pis_prosecution_ledger
title: [? if left_in_government = 0: Put Barski's appointment and disputed instructions on a public ledger?][? if left_in_government = 1: Force our PiS partners to disclose Barski's appointment and disputed instructions?]
subtitle: Spend legal capacity on documents and whistleblower protection; visibility rises, but Barski keeps command.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The party's legal team has no spare capacity to verify and protect the record.
