[? if left_in_government = 0: Lewica's lawyers publish the act restoring
Barski, the competing opinions and a dated register of instructions challenged
by prosecutors below him. Barski remains behind the National Prosecutor's
desk. From now on, however, every official who follows a disputed order knows
that its author and legal basis will appear together in public.?]
[? if left_in_government = 1: At coalition council, Lewica ministers demand the
same papers that PiS expected its partners not to ask for. Justice Minister
**[+ justice_minister +]** yields documents, not command, and Barski remains in
office. The disclosure gives individual prosecutors a record on which to rely;
it also makes Lewica an acknowledged dissenter inside a government whose
orders it still helps sustain.?]

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the ledger

@pis_prosecution_statute
title: [? if left_in_government = 0: Table a law separating the National Prosecutor from the Justice Minister?][? if left_in_government = 1: Bring an independent-prosecution bill from the government benches?]
subtitle: Write appointment, tenure and removal rules into law, though PiS still controls whether the bill receives a majority.
on-arrival: judicial_repair_mandate += 4; constitutional_restraint += 3; pis_relation -= 5; ko_relation += 2; news_headline = "A junior coalition bill challenges PiS prosecutorial command" if left_in_government = 1; news_headline = "An opposition statute records the alternative chain of command" if left_in_government = 0

[? if left_in_government = 0: The bill gives the National Prosecutor a fixed
term, a public appointment procedure and removal only for reasons stated in
law. KO supports its first reading; PiS sends it to a committee it controls.
Barski signs tomorrow's instructions as before, but the alternative is now a
piece of legislation rather than a promise for the next election.?]
[? if left_in_government = 1: Lewica ministers place a bill on the Sejm docket
that would separate their coalition partner's Justice Ministry from day-to-day
prosecutorial command. PiS whips bury it before passage and Kaczyński calls the
move a breach of cabinet solidarity. Barski loses no power; Lewica has at least
made its proposed succession law public while sharing government with the men
who refuse it.?]

- @poland_event_queue: Table the statute

@pis_prosecution_committee
title: [? if left_in_government = 0: Ask KO, PSL and Poland 2050 to build a joint oversight panel?][? if left_in_government = 1: Join the democratic opposition in scrutinising our own cabinet's prosecutors?]
subtitle: A common parliamentary record can make the command answer in public—if the other clubs still trust Lewica enough to share it.
